- Deferred by the user: consolidate document metadata in `mobile-document-route.ts`, `../ProjectView.tsx`, and `../routing/` around one route-admitted presentation; remove the secondary document catalog lookup and redundant retention fields only after local Untitled, viewer, Work and draft-review paths are covered. Preserve phone's distinct UI, single-active-view lifecycle and session-host ownership; do not unify it with desktop. Add phone composition-level transition coverage and a real phone probe. Implementation sequence and acceptance criteria: [#529](https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow/issues/529). Not part of PR #526's current implementation scope.
- Phone review follow-ups (draft review on the phone ships read-only and with a bottom sheet that only closes by its X, its scrim or Escape): (1) an editable review body needs a tap that selects a change without placing a caret, or an explicit "Edit" mode, and the desktop block grip hidden on coarse pointers; (2) swipe-down to dismiss the change sheet; (3) an entry into review from an open live document (desktop uses the identity-bar chip, which the phone shell lacks); open product question, see the [inline track changes decision](https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow-docs/blob/main/kb/decisions/collab/drafts/draft-review-inline-track-changes.md#open-questions); (4) a review that fails to load on the phone shows plain live text with no message, where the desktop host shows "Couldn't open review mode" with Retry and Back to live: give `MobileDocumentReview` the same failure surface.
